SOAP RM (Reliable Messaging) and SOAP 1.x serve different purposes in web services communication:

SOAP 1.x (which includes SOAP 1.1 and SOAP 1.2) is the standard protocol for exchanging structured
information in web services. It supports synchronous and asynchronous communication and is commonly
used for lightweight, stateless interactions.

SOAP RM (Reliable Messaging) is an extension of SOAP that ensures guaranteed message delivery,
even in cases of network failures. It follows WS-ReliableMessaging (WS-RM) standards and includes
features like message persistence, retries, and acknowledgments. It is ideal for scenarios requiring
transactional integrity, such as financial transactions or critical data exchanges



